Task: Kafka produce/consume trace-context propagation (Phase 4a, ADR 0010).

Added purekafka.tracing.KafkaTracing (injectHeaders, traced), mirroring
purerestlib's ClientTracing/ServerTracing shape and reasoning but for
Kafka message headers instead of HTTP headers. Confirmed otel4s's
Tracer[F].propagate/joinOrRoot already resolve an implicit
TextMapGetter/TextMapUpdater for a plain Map[String,String] carrier (same
mechanism the HTTP versions rely on) - no hand-rolled TextMapPropagator
needed, only the carrier representation (fs2-kafka Headers, UTF-8 byte
values via HeaderSerializer.string/HeaderDeserializer.string) is new.
Verified the real fs2-kafka 3.6.0 Header/Headers API via javap against
the resolved jar directly rather than guessing (append takes the
serializer as an implicit parameter, not positional - caught and fixed a
compile error from assuming otherwise). Spans tagged with OpenTelemetry's
messaging.system/messaging.destination.name semantic attributes via
Tracer.spanBuilder(...).addAttributes(...).build.use(...), confirmed via
javap against otel4s-core-trace directly (SpanBuilderMacro.addAttribute(s)).

Files: modules/purekafka/src/main/scala/purekafka/tracing/KafkaTracing.scala (new),
modules/purekafka/src/test/scala/purekafka/tracing/KafkaTracingSuite.scala (new).

Tests: 4 new (inject-with-span, inject-no-span no-op, consumer-span-is-child-of-producer-span,
messaging-semantic-attributes-tagged). All pass.

Deviation: committed Red+Green together, not split into two commits -
both the test and implementation were written together and verified in
one pass, matching Phase 1's commit granularity rather than Phase 2/3's.
